  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this view",
      "items": [
        "Each row is an independent guarded transition, not a chronological sequence across rows. Repeated phase labels name the same underlying phase; aliases prevent unrelated rules from sharing ambiguous drawing corridors. The normal-procedure view supplies the connected happy path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Reading this view",
      "items": [
        "snake_case labels are real session.phase strings. Nodes in the 'conceptual step' legend group, or with tag 'conceptual'/'phase group', are not phase strings.",
        "Pilot calls move a phase only after telemetry confirms the claim (_at_hold, _at_crossing, _lined_up). Take-off, landing and vacating come from the mission track alone (airfield.py 44-50)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Closure rules",
      "items": [
        "A cancel or check-out while occupying a runway sets phase 'cancelled' with vacating. The session is released only once vacating is observed or reported (1540-1543, 1800-1805).",
        "_takeoff always frees only this aircraft's own lane and warns 'takeoff not cleared' unless the phase was cleared_takeoff (906-917).",
        "dead, eject, disconnect and birth events close any session (80-81, 808-810). See the session safeguards view."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Transition evidence (file lines)",
      "items": [
        "startup_requested \u2192 closed: other field or airborne (886-887, 907-909)",
        "startup \u2192 closed: off runway: release (1537-1545)",
        "ground phase \u2192 airborne: any ground phase: warning notice (825-826, 916-917)",
        "airborne \u2192 closed: departure release (819-821)"
      ]
    }
  ]
